## Building on Modern macOS

The original build tools were 32-bit binaries that no longer run on macOS Catalina and later. This fork includes rebuilt 64-bit tools and instructions for getting the project to build on modern Macs.

## Prerequisites

- **Xcode Command Line Tools**: `xcode-select --install`
- **make**: included with Xcode CLT

The assembler (`snap`) and disk imager (`crackle`) in `Build/osx32/` have been replaced with 64-bit x86_64 builds compiled from [adamgreen/snapNcrackle](https://github.com/adamgreen/snapNcrackle). On Apple Silicon Macs, these run via Rosetta 2.

### Rebuilding snap/crackle from source (optional)

Only needed if the included binaries don't work on your system:

```bash
cd /tmp
git clone https://github.com/adamgreen/snapNcrackle.git
cd snapNcrackle
```

Add `-Wno-deprecated-declarations` to `CPPUTEST_WARNINGFLAGS` in `libcommon/makefile`, `libsnap/makefile`, and `libcrackle/makefile`. Also add `-Wno-varargs` to `libcrackle/makefile`. Then:

```bash
make clean all CFG=Release
cp snap/Release/snap /path/to/Prince-of-Persia-Apple-II/Build/osx32/snap
cp crackle/Release/crackle /path/to/Prince-of-Persia-Apple-II/Build/osx32/crackle
```

## Build

```bash
make clean all
```

This produces three disk images:

| File | Format | Size |
|------|--------|------|
| `PrinceOfPersia_3.5.hdv` | 3.5" ProDOS block image | 800 KB |
| `PrinceOfPersia_5.25_SideA.nib` | 5.25" nibble image (Side A) | 228 KB |
| `PrinceOfPersia_5.25_SideB.nib` | 5.25" nibble image (Side B) | 228 KB |

Assembly warnings about `DO/IF` and `fin` directives in GRAFIX.S and SPECIALK.S are expected and harmless.

### Build variants

```bash
make clean all RELEASE_PATCH=1   # Apply release patches (disables cheats, updates version date)
make clean all VERBOSE=1         # Show assembler/imager commands as they run
```

## Running

The 5.25" `.nib` images work in [Virtual II](https://virtualii.com/) (macOS) or any Apple IIe emulator:

1. Configure an **Apple IIe** with two 5.25" floppy drives (Disk II in slot 6)
2. Insert `PrinceOfPersia_5.25_SideA.nib` into Drive 1 and boot
3. When prompted, swap Drive 1 to `PrinceOfPersia_5.25_SideB.nib`

The 3.5" `.hdv` image works with a UniDisk 3.5 drive configuration.

## Controls

Press **Ctrl+K** for keyboard controls, **Ctrl+J** for joystick.

I/K/J/L - Move

U/O - Diagonal Jump

H - Shoot fireball (with every apology possible to Jordan Mechner)

